('source.china.xiyouji.wikisource','Journey to the West (Wikisource transcription, 100 chapters)','西遊記','LITERARY_TEXT_DIGITAL_EDITION',4,'Chinese Wikisource','Attributed to Wu Cheng''en (Ming novel, 16th century); community transcription','lang.zh',NULL,'2026-10-11','https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E8%A5%BF%E9%81%8A%E8%A8%98',NULL,'Xiyouji, chapters 1–100','Public-domain novel; Wikisource transcription under CC BY-SA','Sixteenth-century vernacular novel; a later literary reception layer, not an ancient mythological witness',NULL,'Public web page',0,'Cite chapter numbers; publish independent retellings rather than the transcription.',0,'Vernacular Chinese original','URL_SYNTAX_VALID','Chapter index (第一回 to 第一百回, including 第七回 八卦爐中逃大聖 五行山下定心猿) matched through public search-index metadata on 2026-10-11.'),
('source.china.fengshen_yanyi.wikisource','Investiture of the Gods (Wikisource transcription, 100 chapters)','封神演義','LITERARY_TEXT_DIGITAL_EDITION',4,'Chinese Wikisource','Attributed to Xu Zhonglin or Lu Xixing (Ming novel); community transcription','lang.zh',NULL,'2026-10-11','https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E5%B0%81%E7%A5%9E%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9',NULL,'Fengshen yanyi, 卷001–卷100','Public-domain novel; Wikisource transcription under CC BY-SA','Ming vernacular novel; a later literary reception layer that drew on popular religion',NULL,'Public web page',0,'Cite chapter numbers; publish independent retellings rather than the transcription.',0,'Vernacular Chinese original','URL_SYNTAX_VALID','Chapter pages 卷012 (第十二回 陳塘關哪吒出世) and 卷013 (第十三回 太乙真人收石磯) matched through public search-index metadata on 2026-10-11; 卷014 follows the same pattern.'),
('source.greek.plutarch_isis_osiris.lacuscurtius','Plutarch, On Isis and Osiris (tr. F. C. Babbitt, Loeb Moralia V, 1936)','Περὶ Ἴσιδος καὶ Ὀσίριδος','HISTORICAL_TRANSLATION',3,'LacusCurtius (University of Chicago, Bill Thayer)','Plutarch (c. 46–after 119 CE); translated by Frank Cole Babbitt','lang.en','1936','2026-10-11','https://penelope.uchicago.edu/Thayer/E/Roman/Texts/Plutarch/Moralia/Isis_and_Osiris*/home.html',NULL,'Moralia 351C–384C (De Iside et Osiride), chapters 1–80','Babbitt''s 1936 Loeb translation as transcribed by LacusCurtius, which marks it public domain in the United States','A Greek philosopher''s account of Egyptian myth written about 100 CE; the only connected ancient narrative of the Osiris story, and a later reception layer rather than an Egyptian witness',NULL,'Public web page',0,'Cite chapter numbers; publish independent retellings rather than the translation.',0,'English translation of the Greek','URL_SYNTAX_VALID','LacusCurtius home page for Babbitt''s translation and the parallel Perseus/CTS sections (e.g. ch. 15, the Byblos episode) matched through public search-index metadata on 2026-10-11.'),
('source.indian.ramayana_griffith.gutenberg','The Rámáyan of Válmíki, translated into English verse (R. T. H. Griffith, 1870–1874)','रामायण','HISTORICAL_TRANSLATION',3,'Project Gutenberg (eBook #24869)','Attributed to Vālmīki; translated by Ralph T. H. Griffith','lang.en','1870–1874','2026-10-11','https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/24869',NULL,'Books I–VI (Bāla to Yuddha Kāṇḍa); e.g. Book I, Canto LXVII, The Breaking of the Bow','Public-domain nineteenth-century translation distributed by Project Gutenberg','Nineteenth-century English verse translation of the vulgate Sanskrit text, not the Baroda critical edition; the Rāmāyaṇa is also a living sacred text with many regional and devotional retellings',NULL,'Public web page',0,'Cite book (kāṇḍa) and canto; publish independent retellings rather than the translation; keep other Rāmāyaṇa traditions (Tulsīdās, Kamban and others) separate.',0,'English verse translation of the Sanskrit','URL_SYNTAX_VALID','Project Gutenberg HTML edition of Griffith''s translation and a mirror of the sacred-texts index (Book I, Canto LXVII: The Breaking of the Bow) matched through public search-index metadata on 2026-10-11.');

