('deity.chinese.jade_emperor','Jade Emperor','玉皇大帝','玉皇大帝','Yùhuáng Dàdì','DEITY','civ.chinese_folk','Song–Ming popular religion; Ming novel portrayal','Ruler of the heavenly court in Chinese popular religion; in Journey to the West he tries to appease and then subdue Sun Wukong.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.chinese.erlang_shen','Erlang Shen','二郎神','顯聖二郎真君','Xiǎnshèng Èrláng Zhēnjūn','DEITY','civ.chinese_folk','Popular religion; Ming novel portrayal','The Illustrious Sage Erlang of Guanjiang, the Jade Emperor''s nephew in Journey to the West, who outmatches Sun Wukong in transformations.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.chinese.taishang_laojun','Taishang Laojun','太上老君','太上老君','Tàishàng Lǎojūn','DEITY','civ.daoist','Daoist tradition; Ming novel portrayal','Deified Laozi of Daoist tradition; in Journey to the West he keeps the elixir gourds at the Tushita Palace and refines Sun Wukong in his Eight Trigrams furnace.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.chinese.rulai_xiyouji','Tathāgata Buddha (Journey to the West)','如来佛祖（《西游记》）','如來佛祖','Rúlái Fózǔ','DEITY','civ.chinese_folk','Ming novel portrayal','The novel''s character Rulai, who wagers with Sun Wukong and pins him under the Mountain of Five Elements; kept separate from historical and doctrinal accounts of the Buddha.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"scope": "Novel character; no doctrinal or historical claim about the Buddha"}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.chinese.ao_guang','Ao Guang, Dragon King of the Eastern Sea','东海龙王敖广','東海龍王敖廣','Áo Guǎng','DEITY','civ.chinese_folk',NULL,'Dragon King of the Eastern Sea in Ming novels: he yields the ocean-fixing iron to Sun Wukong in Journey to the West and quarrels with Nezha in Investiture of the Gods.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('hero.chinese.subodhi_patriarch','Patriarch Subodhi','须菩提祖师','須菩提祖師','Xūpútí Zǔshī','HERO','civ.chinese_folk',NULL,'The immortal teacher in Journey to the West who names Sun Wukong and teaches him the seventy-two transformations and the somersault cloud.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"scope": "Novel character"}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('place.chinese.huaguo_shan','Mountain of Flowers and Fruit','花果山','花果山','Huāguǒ Shān','MYTHICAL_PLACE','civ.chinese_folk',NULL,'Mountain in the land of Aolai on the Eastern Continent where the stone monkey is born, with the Water Curtain Cave behind its waterfall.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('event.chinese.havoc_in_heaven','Havoc in Heaven (Journey to the West, chapters 1–7)','大闹天宫（《西游记》第一至七回）',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.chinese_folk',NULL,'The opening arc of Journey to the West: the stone monkey''s birth, training, rebellion against heaven and confinement under the Mountain of Five Elements.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.chinese.li_jing','Li Jing, the Pagoda-Bearing Heavenly King','托塔天王李靖','托塔天王李靖','Tuōtǎ Tiānwáng Lǐ Jìng','DEITY','civ.chinese_folk',NULL,'Commander of Chentang Pass and Nezha''s father in Investiture of the Gods, who receives the golden pagoda that gives him his title; in Journey to the West he leads heaven''s army.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('hero.chinese.taiyi_zhenren','Taiyi Zhenren','太乙真人','太乙真人','Tàiyǐ Zhēnrén','HERO','civ.chinese_folk',NULL,'Immortal of the Golden Light Cave on Qianyuan Mountain in Investiture of the Gods; Nezha''s teacher, who rebuilds his body from lotus.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{"scope": "Novel character"}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('dragon.chinese.ao_bing','Ao Bing, third son of the Dragon King','龙王三太子敖丙','敖丙','Áo Bǐng','DRAGON','civ.chinese_folk',NULL,'Third son of Ao Guang, killed by the child Nezha at the Nine Bends River in Investiture of the Gods ch. 12.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('weapon.chinese.qiankun_quan','Universe Ring (Qiankun quan)','乾坤圈','乾坤圈','Qiánkūn quān','WEAPON','civ.chinese_folk',NULL,'Golden ring on the newborn Nezha''s arm in Investiture of the Gods, which he throws as a weapon.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('artifact.chinese.linglong_pagoda','Golden exquisite pagoda','玲珑宝塔','玲瓏寶塔','Línglóng bǎotǎ','SACRED_OBJECT','civ.chinese_folk',NULL,'Pagoda given to Li Jing by the Daoist Randeng in Investiture of the Gods ch. 14 to subdue Nezha; the origin of the title Pagoda-Bearing Heavenly King.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('event.chinese.nezha_sea_uproar','Nezha Conquers the Sea (Investiture of the Gods ch. 12–14)','哪吒闹海（《封神演义》第十二至十四回）',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.chinese_folk',NULL,'Nezha''s birth, killing of the dragon prince, self-sacrifice to save his parents and rebirth in a lotus body.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.greek.prometheus','Prometheus','普罗米修斯','Προμηθεύς','Promētheus','DEITY','civ.greek','Archaic Greek poetry','Son of Iapetus who outwits Zeus at Mecone and steals fire for mortals in Hesiod''s Theogony (lines 507–616).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('creature.greek.hecatoncheires','Hundred-Handers (Cottus, Briareos and Gyes)','百臂巨人','Ἑκατόγχειρες','Hekatoncheires','GIANT','civ.greek',NULL,'The three hundred-armed, fifty-headed sons of Earth and Heaven whom Zeus frees to win the war against the Titans (Theogony 147–153, 617–735).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('event.greek.theogony_succession','From Chaos to the reign of Zeus (Theogony)','从卡俄斯到宙斯为王（《神谱》）',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.greek',NULL,'Hesiod''s account of the first beings, the overthrow of Ouranos and Cronus, the war with the Titans, Typhoeus and the reign of Zeus.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.norse.hodr','Höðr','霍德尔','Höðr',NULL,'DEITY','civ.norse','Snorri''s Edda (c. 1220)','Blind god who, guided by Loki, throws the mistletoe that kills Baldr (Gylfaginning 49).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.norse.hermod','Hermóðr','赫尔莫德','Hermóðr',NULL,'DEITY','civ.norse','Snorri''s Edda (c. 1220)','Son of Odin who rides Sleipnir nine nights to Hel to ransom Baldr (Gylfaginning 49).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.norse.nanna_nepsdottir','Nanna (wife of Baldr)','南娜（巴德尔之妻）','Nanna Nepsdóttir',NULL,'DEITY','civ.norse','Snorri''s Edda (c. 1220)','Baldr''s wife, whose heart bursts with grief at his funeral (Gylfaginning 49); distinct from the Sumerian moon god Nanna.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.norse.sigyn','Sigyn','西格恩','Sigyn',NULL,'DEITY','civ.norse','Snorri''s Edda (c. 1220)','Loki''s wife, who holds a bowl to catch the serpent''s venom over the bound Loki (Gylfaginning 50).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.norse.skadi','Skaði','斯卡蒂','Skaði',NULL,'DEITY','civ.norse','Snorri''s Edda (c. 1220)','Giantess counted among the goddesses; she fastens a venomous snake above the bound Loki (Gylfaginning 50).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('being.norse.utgarda_loki','Útgarða-Loki','乌特加尔洛基','Útgarða-Loki',NULL,'GIANT','civ.norse',NULL,'Giant king of Útgarðr who deceives Thor with illusions and reveals them only as Thor leaves (Gylfaginning 44–47).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('hero.norse.thjalfi','Þjálfi','夏尔菲','Þjálfi',NULL,'HERO','civ.norse',NULL,'Farmer''s son who becomes Thor''s servant after breaking the goat''s thigh bone, and races Hugi at Útgarðr (Gylfaginning 44–46).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('creature.norse.sleipnir','Sleipnir','斯莱布尼尔','Sleipnir',NULL,'DIVINE_BEAST','civ.norse',NULL,'Odin''s eight-legged horse, ridden by Hermóðr on the journey to Hel (Gylfaginning 49).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('event.norse.thor_utgard','Thor''s journey to Útgarða-Loki','索尔前往乌特加尔洛基之城',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.norse',NULL,'Thor, Loki and Þjálfi travel to Útgarðr, lose every contest to illusions, and learn the truth as they leave (Gylfaginning 44–47).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('hero.mesopotamian.enkidu','Enkidu','恩奇都','Enkidu','Enkidu','HERO','civ.babylonian','Standard Babylonian epic (late 2nd–1st millennium BCE)','Wild man fashioned from clay by the goddess Aruru as Gilgamesh''s equal; his friendship and death drive the Standard Babylonian epic.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('hero.mesopotamian.utnapishtim','Uta-napishti','乌特纳皮什提','Ūta-napišti','Uta-napishti','HERO','civ.babylonian',NULL,'Survivor of the Flood granted eternal life by the gods, who tells Gilgamesh the Flood story in Tablet XI.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('creature.mesopotamian.bull_of_heaven','Bull of Heaven','天牛',NULL,NULL,'MONSTER','civ.babylonian',NULL,'Bull that Ishtar obtains from Anu to punish Gilgamesh; killed by Gilgamesh and Enkidu in Tablet VI.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.akkadian.shamash','Shamash','沙玛什','Šamaš','Shamash','DEITY','civ.akkadian',NULL,'Akkadian sun god who protects Gilgamesh and sends thirteen winds against Humbaba; the Akkadian counterpart of Sumerian Utu, kept as a separate entity.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.babylonian.apsu','Apsû','阿普苏','Apsû',NULL,'PRIMORDIAL_DEITY','civ.babylonian',NULL,'Primordial fresh water, begetter of the gods with Tiamat in Enūma eliš, slain by Ea.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.babylonian.ea','Ea (Nudimmud)','埃阿（努迪穆德）','Ea',NULL,'DEITY','civ.babylonian',NULL,'Wise god who slays Apsû, fathers Marduk and creates humankind from Kingu''s blood in Enūma eliš; the Akkadian name associated with Sumerian Enki, kept as a separate entity.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.babylonian.kingu','Qingu','金古','Qingu',NULL,'DEITY','civ.babylonian',NULL,'Tiamat''s champion, given the Tablet of Destinies; after his defeat humankind is made from his blood (Enūma eliš IV, VI).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.sumerian.ninshubur','Ninšubur','宁舒布尔','Ninšubur',NULL,'DEITY','civ.sumerian',NULL,'Inana''s minister, who laments for her and seeks help from Enlil, Nanna and Enki in Inana''s Descent.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.sumerian.dumuzi','Dumuzid','杜木兹','Dumuzid',NULL,'DEITY','civ.sumerian',NULL,'Inana''s husband, handed to the demons as her substitute in Inana''s Descent.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('event.babylonian.gilgamesh_epic','The Standard Babylonian Epic of Gilgamesh','标准巴比伦版吉尔伽美什史诗',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.babylonian',NULL,'From the oppression of Uruk and the friendship with Enkidu to the Flood story and the lost plant of rejuvenation (Tablets I–XI).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.japanese.ame_no_uzume','Ame-no-Uzume','天宇受卖命','天宇受賣命','Ame-no-Uzume-no-mikoto','DEITY','civ.japanese_shinto','Kojiki (712 CE)','Kami whose possessed dance before the Heavenly Rock-Dwelling makes the eight hundred myriad deities laugh and draws Amaterasu out (Kojiki, Sect. XVI).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.japanese.omoikane','Omoikane','思金神','思金神','Omoikane-no-kami','DEITY','civ.japanese_shinto','Kojiki (712 CE)','Child of Takami-musubi whom the assembled deities ask to devise the plan that brings Amaterasu out of the Heavenly Rock-Dwelling (Kojiki, Sect. XVI).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.japanese.ame_no_tajikarao','Ame-no-Tajikarao','天手力男神','天手力男神','Ame-no-Tajikarao-no-kami','DEITY','civ.japanese_shinto','Kojiki (712 CE)','Kami of great strength who hides beside the door of the Heavenly Rock-Dwelling and draws Amaterasu out by the hand (Kojiki, Sect. XVI).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.japanese.kushinadahime','Kushinadahime','栉名田比卖','櫛名田比賣','Kushinadahime','DEITY','civ.japanese_shinto','Kojiki (712 CE)','Youngest daughter of Ashinazuchi and Tenazuchi in Izumo, saved from the eight-forked serpent by Susanoo, who becomes her husband (Kojiki, Sect. XVIII–XIX).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.japanese.ogetsuhime','Ōgetsuhime','大宜都比卖','大宜都比賣','Ōgetsuhime','DEITY','civ.japanese_shinto','Kojiki (712 CE)','Food goddess killed by Susanoo after his expulsion; silkworms, rice, millet, beans and barley grow from her body (Kojiki, Sect. XVII).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('event.japanese.ame_no_iwato','Amaterasu hides in the Heavenly Rock-Dwelling','天之岩户：天照大神隐入岩屋',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.japanese_shinto',NULL,'Amaterasu shuts herself in the Heavenly Rock-Dwelling after Susanoo''s ravages; the deities'' assembly, mirror, jewels and Ame-no-Uzume''s dance bring her out (Kojiki, Sect. XV–XVI).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.hindu.rama','Rāma','罗摩','राम','Rāma','DEITY','civ.hindu','Vālmīki Rāmāyaṇa (composed c. 5th century BCE–1st century CE, dates debated)','Prince of Ayodhyā and hero of Vālmīki''s Rāmāyaṇa, revered in Hindu tradition as an avatar of Vishnu.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.hindu.sita','Sītā','悉多','सीता','Sītā','DEITY','civ.hindu','Vālmīki Rāmāyaṇa','Daughter of King Janaka, found in a ploughed furrow, wife of Rāma; revered in Hindu tradition as a form of Lakṣmī.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('deity.hindu.hanuman','Hanumān','哈奴曼','हनुमान्','Hanumān','DEITY','civ.hindu','Vālmīki Rāmāyaṇa','Vānara son of the wind god and minister of Sugrīva, who leaps the sea to Laṅkā, finds Sītā and burns the city; worshipped widely as a deity of devotion and strength.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('hero.indian.lakshmana','Lakṣmaṇa','罗什曼那','लक्ष्मण','Lakṣmaṇa','HERO','civ.hindu',NULL,'Rāma''s younger half-brother and constant companion in exile, who slays Indrajit in the war at Laṅkā.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('hero.indian.dasharatha','Daśaratha','十车王','दशरथ','Daśaratha','HERO','civ.hindu',NULL,'King of Ayodhyā and father of Rāma, bound by two boons to Kaikeyī; he dies of grief after Rāma''s exile.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('hero.indian.bharata','Bharata','婆罗多（罗摩之弟）','भरत','Bharata','HERO','civ.hindu',NULL,'Son of Kaikeyī who refuses the throne won for him and rules Ayodhyā in the name of Rāma''s sandals.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('demon.hindu.ravana','Rāvaṇa','罗波那','रावण','Rāvaṇa','DEMON','civ.hindu',NULL,'Ten-headed rākṣasa king of Laṅkā, protected by Brahmā''s boon from gods and demons, who abducts Sītā and is slain by Rāma.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('place.hindu.lanka','Laṅkā (Rāmāyaṇa)','楞伽城（《罗摩衍那》）',NULL,NULL,'MYTHICAL_PLACE','civ.hindu',NULL,'Golden island city of Rāvaṇa across the southern sea in the Rāmāyaṇa; its identification with modern places is a matter of later tradition and debate.','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z'),
('event.hindu.sita_abduction_rescue','Abduction and rescue of Sītā (Rāmāyaṇa)','悉多被劫与救回（《罗摩衍那》）',NULL,NULL,'EVENT','civ.hindu',NULL,'From Rāma''s exile and Rāvaṇa''s abduction of Sītā to the bridge to Laṅkā, the war and Rāma''s coronation (Books II–VI).','PARTIAL','SOURCE_BACKED',1,'{}','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z','2026-10-11T01:00:00Z');

